    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nI am getting this error when trying to use the text objects. I cannot reproduce with minimal config, so something must be conflicting with the plugin. I previously used targets.vim and I am hoping to replace with mini.ai.\r\n\r\nI understand it may not technically be a bug, I'm just hoping someone can point me in the right direction to figure out what might be causing this error:\r\n\r\n```\r\nE5108: Error executing lua /home/nick/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.ai/lua/mini/ai.lua:1584: bad argument #2 to 'next_span' (number expected, got string)\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        [C]: in function 'next_span'\r\n        /home/nick/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.ai/lua/mini/ai.lua:1584: in function 'process'\r\n        /home/nick/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.ai/lua/mini/ai.lua:1607: in function 'iterate_matched_spans'\r\n        /home/nick/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.ai/lua/mini/ai.lua:1560: in function 'find_best_match'\r\n        /home/nick/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.ai/lua/mini/ai.lua:1374: in function 'find_next'\r\n        /home/nick/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.ai/lua/mini/ai.lua:1396: in function 'find_textobject_region'\r\n        /home/nick/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.ai/lua/mini/ai.lua:560: in function 'find_textobject'\r\n        /home/nick/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.ai/lua/mini/ai.lua:983: in function 'select_textobject'\r\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\r\n```\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.9.0-dev-1170+gb9f19d3e2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Type `vaf`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nExpect it to select the next function as it does with minimal config\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nImmediately get error message above",
