            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Great!\r\n\r\nLet's now try to be on the same page regarding plugin install:\r\n- Execute `mkdir -p ~/.config/nvim/pack/plugins/opt` . This will create directory where we will install 'mini.ai'.\r\n- Clone 'mini.ai' into that directory with this command:\r\n```bash\r\ngit clone --depth 1 https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.ai.git ~/.config/nvim/pack/plugins/opt/mini.ai\r\n```\r\n- Create an init file (lets say at location '~/init-ai.lua') with the following content:\r\n```lua\r\nvim.cmd('set packpath+=~/.config/nvim')\r\nvim.cmd('packadd mini.ai')\r\n\r\nrequire('mini.ai').setup()\r\n```\r\n- Run Neovim 0.8.3 from appimage you downloaded earlier using the following command (assuming you used '~/init-ai.lua' as file path from previous step):\r\n```bash\r\n<path-to-nvim.appimage> --clean -u ~/init-ai.lua -- ~/init-ai.lua\r\n```\r\n    This should open Neovim with already loaded 'mini.ai' and display initialization file used.\r\n- Try pressing `vaf`. It should select whole first line without errors.",
