            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Sorry if I wasn't clear. I've already tested with minimal config and was **not** able to reproduce the error. It worked exactly as you suggest. I just can't figure out what could possibly be in my config that could interfere with it. I performed your test just to double-check and it highlighted the first line with no errors.\r\n\r\nI am extremely puzzled by this. If 'mini.ai' works on its own, but not inside your configuration (even when it is the only plugin enabled), then it might be some option which does this. After re-reading 'mini.ai' relevant parts of source code several times I can't see how any option can result into an error.\r\n\r\nI'd suggest then going the good old \"bisect by comment out parts of you config\". Like comment all config except 'mini.ai' (which *should* work); uncomment half of your non-plugin config and see if error appears; etc.\r\n\r\nIs [this 'nvim' directory](https://github.com/comfortablynick/dotfiles/tree/main/.config/nvim) in your dotfiles up to date? And do you use regular 'init.lua' and not the 'minit.{lua,vim}' files?",
