        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The reason you have this error is because [you redefine `__call` for string objects](https://github.com/comfortablynick/dotfiles/blob/6e9c5dd4cdab57eec46f9a9b8fbdb747f08764f5/.config/nvim/lua/globals.lua#L100-L110).\r\n\r\nThis conflicts with 'mini.ai' finding logic because [it allows both string patterns and callables](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/doc/mini-ai.txt#L287) to be part of its specification.\r\n\r\nMy only suggestion here would be to not modify built-in Lua tables and use separate helper functions.",
            "created_at": "2023-03-14T10:21:36Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/267#issuecomment-1467814456",
            "id": 1467814456,
